Explanation:
- The primary structure interacts with all other components as it provides the main framework for the CubeSat.
- The secondary structure interacts with the payload, communication system, power system, and attitude control system as it supports these components. It does not directly interact with the primary structure (assuming that the primary structure is the one carrying major loads). However, this interaction could be considered as 1 depending on the specific design of the CubeSat.
- The payload interacts with the communication system and power system to send and receive data and operate accordingly. It does not directly interact with the attitude control system (assuming that the attitude control system is only responsible for maintaining the orientation of the satellite). However, this interaction could be considered as 1 depending on the specific design of the CubeSat.
- The communication system interacts with all other components to send and receive data and commands.
- The power system interacts with all other components to provide them with energy.
- The attitude control system interacts with all other components to maintain the orientation of the satellite.
