- The secondary structure interacts with the payload, power system, and communication system but may not directly interact with the attitude determination and control system (ADCS).
- The payload interacts with the power system and communication system to send data back to Earth. It also interacts with the ADCS for proper orientation during operation.
- The power system provides energy to all other components, including the primary structure, secondary structure, payload, communication system, and ADCS.
- The communication system sends and receives signals from Earth and may interact with the ADCS for antenna pointing.
- The attitude determination and control system interacts with the payload and communication system for proper orientation during operation. It also interacts with the power system to manage its energy consumption.
